WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.112
The tokenizer playground gives a quick visual preview of how text can be split into pieces.

00:00:06.112 --> 00:00:15.407
The I D's in the browser demo are only examples, so use the Python tokenizer when you want the real checkpoint-specific

00:00:15.407 --> 00:00:23.177
tokens. Try punctuation, technical words, U R L's, or code and watch how the pieces change.

00:00:23.177 --> 00:00:31.937
Try a normal sentence first, then something unusual like an email address, a U R L, or a Python variable.

00:00:31.937 --> 00:00:35.483
The differences make tokenization much more intuitive.
